{'symbol': 'AMZN', 'date': '2022-03-15 08:55:00', 'title': 'AMAZON COMMITS $42.5 MILLION TO CREATE MORE THAN 300 NEW AFFORDABLE HOMES NEAR LIGHT RAIL STATIONS IN THE PUGET SOUND REGION', 'text': "SEATTLE--(BUSINESS WIRE)--TODAY AMAZON (NASDAQ: AMZN) ANNOUNCED IT WILL INVEST MORE THAN $42.5 MILLION TO BUILD 318 AFFORDABLE HOMES ADJACENT TO PUBLIC TRANSIT SITES, AND IT WILL WORK IN PARTNERSHIP WITH SOUND TRANSIT, THE TRANSIT SYSTEM SERVING THE CENTRAL PUGET SOUND REGION OF WASHINGTON STATE, TO COMPLETE THE HOUSING DEVELOPMENTS. THE DEALS STEM FROM AMAZON'S $300 MILLION TRANSIT COMMITMENT FROM 2021 TO CREATE 3,000 NEW AFFORDABLE HOMES IN COLLABORATION WITH THE TRANSIT AGENCIES IN AMAZON'S"}